title: Data model
kind: overview
summary: Repositories hold metarecords; a metarecord is a uuid and a multi-map of typed fields; that is the whole model.

Everything metafolder stores fits in three notions:

* a ''repository'' ([[Repository]]) — one directory tree and its own store;
* ''metarecords'' ([[Metarecord]]) — each a set of metadata about one subject, usually a file, identified by a uuid;
* ''fields'' ([[Fields and values]]) — the metadata itself: a name and a typed value, several fields of the same name allowed.

A file is not special: it is a metarecord whose `mfr_path` field places it in the
filesystem's tree ([[Reserved fields]]). A tag, a collection, a duplicate group are
metarecords too, with no file behind them. Fields that point at other metarecords
(`ref`, `tree_ref`) are what links them; `tree_ref` fields arrange them in trees
([[TreeRef forest]]).

